## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical demand-paging and race-free lazy loading in a tiny OS, focusing on synchronization, eviction, and correctness under contention.

## Key Concepts
- Per-page locking and atomic state
- Race-free page-in path and wakeups
- Simple eviction policy under frame pressure
- PTE updates and TLB consistency

## Code Example
```c
// skeleton: per-page fault path
typedef struct { int frame; int valid; int ref; int lock; } PTE;
PTE page_table[NPAGES];
void handle_fault(vaddr_t va){
  pte_t *p = &page_table[PAGE_INDEX(va)];
  while (atomic_test_and_set(&p->lock)) { ; }
  if (!p->valid) { /* choose victim, load page, update p */ }
  p->valid = 1; atomic_clear(&p->lock);
  wake_waiters(p);
}
```

